# What `npx vercel --prod` does NOT upload when it is run from the repo root.
# The website is built from /mobile only (Vercel project root = mobile, build = npm run build:web). Everything else, and everything that is
# rebuilt on Vercel anyway (node_modules, the native Android project, old builds), stays on this computer. Without this file the upload was over 2 GB.
.git
**/node_modules
/backend
/superadmin
/deploy
/docs
/source-art
/netlify.toml
/mobile/android
/mobile/dist
/mobile/dist-web
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/.vercel
.vercel
.env
.env.*
*.env
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
